--- tensor -- host-side dense n-d tensor functions (f64, row-major).
---
--- Single source of truth for the `tensor` host-function surface: 28 ops
--- covering construction (`zeros`, `ones`, `from_list`), projection
--- (`shape`, `to_list`), algebra (`add`/`mul`/`sub`/`div`, `matmul`,
--- `conv2d`, `max_pool`, `batch_norm`), shape manipulation (`reshape`,
--- `transpose`, `concat`), and derivatives (`derive` + the seven
--- `*_backward` adjoints it resolves). A *runtime* (catopt
--- is the first consumer) composes this package by building a `HandlModule`
--- with the Rust `OpRegistry` this repo ships (`tensor_op_registry`), so
--- the `tensor.*` string callees resolve to native impls; nothing in the
--- eval engine or language data knows what a tensor is.
---
--- The tensor value is data on the `serde_json::Value` boundary —
--- `{"__tensor__": {"shape": [d, ...], "data": [x, ...], "dtype": "f64"}}`
--- — following the `{"__bytes__": ...}` tagged convention (ADR-0083 §2.1).
--- `shape` is the extent per axis, `data` the flat row-major payload whose
--- length is the product of `shape`, `dtype` the element type (only `f64`
--- for now). The tag keeps a tensor unambiguous next to user records:
--- engines with the kernel `TaggedValue::Tensor` decode it at the
--- `call_host` boundary and carry it opaquely; engines without it see a
--- plain object — the wire shape is the same either way.
---
--- All 28 functions are FFI atoms: a tensor has no literal syntax and no
--- eval-vocabulary constructor, so construction, projection, and algebra
--- cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows. The `op`/`handle` declaration
--- form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust `Function`
--- impls in `src/ops/` provide the logic and are registered in an
--- `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native impl.
---
--- `tensor.from_list(xs)` infers the shape from nested number arrays and
--- rejects ragged input; the elementwise four (`add`/`mul`/`sub`/`div`)
--- broadcast numpy-style — trailing dims align, a `1`-dim stretches, a
--- missing leading dim counts as `1`; `tensor.matmul(a, b)` is `(m×k)·
--- (k×n)` for rank-2 operands and batched `[B, m, k] × [B, k, n]` for
--- rank-3, with the batch dim broadcasting (a rank-2 side or `B = 1`
--- repeats across the other's batches).
---
--- `conv2d` / `batch_norm` take *positional optional* trailing
--- parameters: a `null` (or a missing argument) selects the default, so
--- `conv2d(x, w, null, [2, 2])` is "no bias, stride 2×2, no padding" and
--- `batch_norm(x, g, b, m, v)` uses the default `eps = 1e-5`. Both are
--- NCHW: `conv2d` consumes `input [N, C_in, H, W]` × `weight
--- [C_out, C_in/groups, kH, kW]` (naive cross-correlation — no kernel
--- flip — with `bias?` rank-1 `[C_out]`, `stride?`/`padding?` an int or
--- `[h, w]` pair, `groups?` a positive int); `batch_norm` is the
--- eval-mode `(x − μ)/√(σ²+ε)·γ+β` per channel with rank-1 `[C]`
--- `gamma`/`beta`/`mean`/`var` parameters. `max_pool(input, kernel,
--- stride?)` is NCHW max pooling with the same int-or-pair convention
--- for `kernel`/`stride` (stride defaults to the kernel); the output
--- drops trailing partial windows (floor mode).
---
--- The shape-manipulation three re-label rather than learn semantics:
--- `reshape(t, shape)` keeps the row-major payload and requires the new
--- extents' product to equal the element count (no `-1` wildcard);
--- `transpose(t, d0, d1)` swaps two axes; `concat(xs, axis)` joins a
--- non-empty list of same-rank tensors that agree on every axis but
--- `axis`, whose extents sum.
---
--- `tensor.derive(name)` returns the qualified op name of the adjoint
--- registered for `name` (qualified or bare local), or `null` when no
--- pair exists — a *registered-pairs* table, not autodiff: a `.hnl`
--- function name gets `null` since a host `Function` sees only
--- evaluated argument values. Seven pairs so far: the elementwise four
--- and `matmul` map to `(a, b, grad_out) -> {"a", "b"}` adjoints that
--- sum broadcast dims back to each operand's shape; `conv2d` maps to
--- `conv2d_backward(input, weight, grad_out, bias?, stride?, padding?,
--- groups?) -> {"input", "weight", "bias"?}`; and `batch_norm` maps to
--- `batch_norm_backward(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, grad_out, eps?)`
--- which returns the differentiable inputs' grads `{"input": dx,
--- "gamma": dγ, "beta": dβ}` (mean/var are statistical in eval mode
--- and carry none). The `*_backward` convention: required primal args,
--- then the upstream gradient, then the primal's positional optionals.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- tensor.zeros -- a tensor of `shape` filled with 0.0.
--- tensor.ones -- a tensor of `shape` filled with 1.0.
--- tensor.from_list -- a tensor whose flat row-major data is `xs`' nested number arrays (ragged rejected).
--- tensor.to_list -- the nested number arrays for tensor `t` (inverse of from_list).
--- tensor.shape -- the extent-per-axis list of tensor `t`.
--- tensor.add -- elementwise `a + b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.add_backward -- adjoint of `add`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}` (broadcast grads sum back).
--- tensor.mul -- elementwise `a * b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.mul_backward -- adjoint of `mul`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}`.
--- tensor.sub -- elementwise `a - b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.sub_backward -- adjoint of `sub`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}`.
--- tensor.div -- elementwise `a / b` (numpy-style broadcasting).
--- tensor.div_backward -- adjoint of `div`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}`.
--- tensor.matmul -- `(m×k)·(k×n)` dense matrix product; rank-3 sides batch over `B` (batch broadcasts).
--- tensor.matmul_backward -- adjoint of `matmul`: `(a, b, grad_out) -> {a, b}` (`g·bᵀ`, `aᵀ·g`).
--- tensor.conv2d -- NCHW conv2d `(input, weight, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?)`.
--- tensor.conv2d_backward -- adjoint of `conv2d`: `(input, weight, grad_out, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?) -> {input, weight, bias?}`.
--- tensor.max_pool -- NCHW max pooling `(input, kernel, stride?)`; stride defaults to kernel.
--- tensor.batch_norm -- eval-mode batch norm `(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, eps?)`.
--- tensor.reshape -- `t` re-labeled under `shape` (product must equal the element count).
--- tensor.transpose -- `t` with axes `d0`/`d1` swapped.
--- tensor.concat -- `xs` joined along `axis` (same rank, other axes equal).
--- tensor.batch_norm_backward -- adjoint of `tensor.batch_norm`: `(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, grad_out, eps?) -> {input, gamma, beta}`.
--- tensor.derive -- the adjoint op name registered for `name` (qualified or bare local), or `null`.
cap "tensor.zeros"
cap "tensor.ones"
cap "tensor.from_list"
cap "tensor.to_list"
cap "tensor.shape"
cap "tensor.add"
cap "tensor.add_backward"
cap "tensor.mul"
cap "tensor.mul_backward"
cap "tensor.sub"
cap "tensor.sub_backward"
cap "tensor.div"
cap "tensor.div_backward"
cap "tensor.matmul"
cap "tensor.matmul_backward"
cap "tensor.conv2d"
cap "tensor.conv2d_backward"
cap "tensor.max_pool"
cap "tensor.max_pool_backward"
cap "tensor.batch_norm"
cap "tensor.reshape"
cap "tensor.reshape_backward"
cap "tensor.transpose"
cap "tensor.transpose_backward"
cap "tensor.concat"
cap "tensor.concat_backward"
cap "tensor.batch_norm_backward"
cap "tensor.derive"
op "tensor.zeros" : (List Int) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.ones" : (List Int) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.from_list" : Array -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.to_list" : Tensor -> Array
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.shape" : Tensor -> (List Int)
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.add" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- add_backward(a, b, grad_out) -> {a: da, b: db}, each unbroadcast to
--- the operand's shape.
op "tensor.add_backward" : (Tensor * Tensor * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.mul" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- mul_backward(a, b, grad_out): da = g·b, db = g·a, unbroadcast.
op "tensor.mul_backward" : (Tensor * Tensor * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.sub" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- sub_backward(a, b, grad_out): da = g, db = −g, unbroadcast.
op "tensor.sub_backward" : (Tensor * Tensor * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.div" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- div_backward(a, b, grad_out): da = g/b, db = −g·a/b², unbroadcast.
op "tensor.div_backward" : (Tensor * Tensor * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.matmul" : (Tensor * Tensor) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- matmul_backward(a, b, grad_out): da = g·bᵀ, db = aᵀ·g per batch,
--- unbroadcast over `B` to each operand's shape.
op "tensor.matmul_backward" : (Tensor * Tensor * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
--- conv2d(input, weight, bias?, stride?, padding?, groups?) — variadic;
--- `null` at an optional position selects the default (see the header).
op "tensor.conv2d" : Value... -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- conv2d_backward(input, weight, grad_out, bias?, stride?, padding?,
--- groups?) — required primal args, then grad_out, then the primal's
--- optionals in order; returns {input, weight, bias?}.
op "tensor.conv2d_backward" : Value... -> Value
  guarantee: True
--- max_pool(input, kernel, stride?) — variadic; `null` `stride` selects
--- the kernel as the stride. Floor mode: trailing partial windows drop.
op "tensor.max_pool" : Value... -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- max_pool_backward(input, grad_out, kernel, stride?, padding?):
--- each grad scatters to its window's argmax; returns {input}.
op "tensor.max_pool_backward" : Value... -> Value
  guarantee: True
--- batch_norm(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, eps?) — variadic; `null`
--- `eps` selects the 1e-5 default.
op "tensor.batch_norm" : Value... -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.reshape" : (Tensor * (List Int)) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- reshape_backward(input, shape, grad_out) -> {input}.
op "tensor.reshape_backward" : (Tensor * (List Int) * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.transpose" : (Tensor * Int * Int) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- transpose_backward(input, d0, d1, grad_out) -> {input}.
op "tensor.transpose_backward" : (Tensor * Int * Int * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.concat" : (Array * Int) -> Tensor
  guarantee: True
--- concat_backward(xs, axis, grad_out) -> {xs: per-input slices}.
op "tensor.concat_backward" : (Array * Int * Tensor) -> Value
  guarantee: True
--- batch_norm_backward(input, gamma, beta, mean, var, grad_out, eps?) —
--- primal signature + upstream grad → {input, gamma, beta} grads.
op "tensor.batch_norm_backward" : Value... -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "tensor.derive" : String -> Value
  guarantee: True
handle "tensor.zeros" with rust_tensor_zeros
handle "tensor.ones" with rust_tensor_ones
handle "tensor.from_list" with rust_tensor_from_list
handle "tensor.to_list" with rust_tensor_to_list
handle "tensor.shape" with rust_tensor_shape
handle "tensor.add" with rust_tensor_add
handle "tensor.add_backward" with rust_tensor_add_backward
handle "tensor.mul" with rust_tensor_mul
handle "tensor.mul_backward" with rust_tensor_mul_backward
handle "tensor.sub" with rust_tensor_sub
handle "tensor.sub_backward" with rust_tensor_sub_backward
handle "tensor.div" with rust_tensor_div
handle "tensor.div_backward" with rust_tensor_div_backward
handle "tensor.matmul" with rust_tensor_matmul
handle "tensor.matmul_backward" with rust_tensor_matmul_backward
handle "tensor.conv2d" with rust_tensor_conv2d
handle "tensor.conv2d_backward" with rust_tensor_conv2d_backward
handle "tensor.max_pool" with rust_tensor_max_pool
handle "tensor.max_pool_backward" with rust_tensor_max_pool_backward
handle "tensor.batch_norm" with rust_tensor_batch_norm
handle "tensor.reshape" with rust_tensor_reshape
handle "tensor.reshape_backward" with rust_tensor_reshape_backward
handle "tensor.transpose" with rust_tensor_transpose
handle "tensor.transpose_backward" with rust_tensor_transpose_backward
handle "tensor.concat" with rust_tensor_concat
handle "tensor.concat_backward" with rust_tensor_concat_backward
handle "tensor.batch_norm_backward" with rust_tensor_batch_norm_backward
handle "tensor.derive" with rust_tensor_derive

--- The `tensor` namespace record — `from "host-tensor" import tensor` binds
--- the whole surface at once (each field is the qualified-name string the
--- `op` declarations export, so `tensor.matmul(a, b)` dispatches through
--- `call_host` exactly like the per-name imports do).
export tensor := {
  zeros: "tensor.zeros",
  ones: "tensor.ones",
  from_list: "tensor.from_list",
  to_list: "tensor.to_list",
  shape: "tensor.shape",
  add: "tensor.add",
  add_backward: "tensor.add_backward",
  mul: "tensor.mul",
  mul_backward: "tensor.mul_backward",
  sub: "tensor.sub",
  sub_backward: "tensor.sub_backward",
  div: "tensor.div",
  div_backward: "tensor.div_backward",
  matmul: "tensor.matmul",
  matmul_backward: "tensor.matmul_backward",
  conv2d: "tensor.conv2d",
  conv2d_backward: "tensor.conv2d_backward",
  max_pool: "tensor.max_pool",
  max_pool_backward: "tensor.max_pool_backward",
  batch_norm: "tensor.batch_norm",
  reshape: "tensor.reshape",
  reshape_backward: "tensor.reshape_backward",
  transpose: "tensor.transpose",
  transpose_backward: "tensor.transpose_backward",
  concat: "tensor.concat",
  concat_backward: "tensor.concat_backward",
  batch_norm_backward: "tensor.batch_norm_backward",
    derive: "tensor.derive"
}
